course: dictionary
lesson: 6665
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «In one myth a nymph called Syrinx ran from Pan and was turned into reeds by a river.» Myths are old stories, and here a nymph is a nature spirit, not a bug.
explain: Now read «Dragonfly nymphs live underwater.» This is a science sentence. A nymph is a young insect, with no wings yet, that will grow into an adult. The clues are dragonfly and underwater.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A nature spirit could live by a river, but a nature spirit would not grow into a dragonfly. If your meaning does not fit, try the other meaning.
fact: A nymph is a nature spirit in Greek and Roman myths, and it looks like a young woman.
fact: In these stories, nymphs live in forests, rivers, seas and mountains.
fact: In science, a nymph is the young form of some insects, such as dragonflies and grasshoppers.
fact: A nymph looks a bit like the adult insect, but it has no wings yet.
fact: «Mayflies live a year or more as nymphs under water», then become adults that live only a day or two.
exercise: «In one myth a nymph called Syrinx ran from Pan.» In this sentence, what is a nymph? | *A nature spirit who looks like a young woman | A kind of fish | A type of tree | A young insect with no wings yet
exercise: «Dragonfly nymphs live underwater.» In this sentence, what is a nymph? | A grown-up dragonfly with bright wings | *A young insect with no wings yet | A small frog | A nature spirit who looks like a young woman
exercise: In Greek and Roman myths, where would you find a nymph? | Inside a computer | *A forest, a river, a sea or a mountain | A kitchen cupboard | A school classroom
test: Ella reads, «Grasshopper nymphs climb up a grass stalk.» Which meaning fits here? | A grown-up grasshopper with wings | A green plant | A nature spirit in a myth | *A young grasshopper with no wings yet
test: Why do the words around a word help you? | They are always wrong | They stop you reading on | They make the sentence longer | *They show which meaning the writer means
exam: «Mayflies live a year or more as nymphs under water, then as adults for only a day or two.» What does nymph mean in this sentence? | A kind of cloud | *A young insect that lives in water | A tree in a forest | A nature spirit in a myth
